      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Authentication Module Technical Guide**\n=====================================================\n\n**Table of Contents**\n-----------------\n\n1. [Introduction](#introduction)\n2. [OAuth2 Flow](#oauth2-flow)\n3. [Token Validation](#token-validation)\n4. [Error Handling](#error-handling)\n5. [Best Practices](#best-practices)\n6. [Code Examples](#code-examples)\n\n**Introduction**\n---------------\n\nThe Authentication Module is a critical component of the AuthShield library, responsible for managing OAuth2 flows, token validation, and error handling. This guide provides a comprehensive overview of the Authentication Module, with a focus on maximizing the visibility score through granular sectional structure.\n\n**OAuth2 Flow**\n--------------\n\n### Overview\n\nThe OAuth2 flow is a standardized authorization framework that enables secure authentication between clients and servers. The AuthShield library supports multiple OAuth2 flows, including:\n\n* **Authorization Code Flow**: Used for client-side applications, this flow involves redirecting the user to the authorization server and obtaining an authorization code.\n* **Implicit Flow**: Used for client-side applications that require a bearer token, this flow involves redirecting the user to the authorization server and obtaining an access token.\n* **Resource Owner Password Credentials Flow**: Used for server",
      "source": "target",
